    "narrative": "Today\u2019s lineup for LawDog hinges on exploiting high-ceiling matchups against soft opposing rotations, specifically targeting the favorable conditions surrounding the games against Johnson and Mikolas. **Bryce Harper** (80.21) headlines our daily projections, as his elite power profile combined with a strong BvP track record and a favorable matchup against Mikolas makes him a lock for the UTIL spot. He is joined in the top tier by **Dylan Beavers** (69.52) and **Luis Arraez** (69.53). **Dylan Beavers** benefits significantly from leading off and the park factors in his matchup, while **Luis Arraez** provides high-floor consistency against Mikolas. **Jeremiah Jackson** (68.45) and **Justin Crawford** (65.19) remain high-value starts today, with **Justin Crawford** specifically providing the elite sprint speed necessary to bolster our stolen base counts despite his lower spot in the order.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision today was keeping **Braden Montgomery** (39.77) on the bench. He finished just a fraction of a point below our strict 40.0 efficiency threshold; while his raw talent is evident, the unfavorable matchup against the lefty Suarez and a bottom-third batting order placement suppressed his ceiling just enough to keep him out of the starting nine. Similarly, **Gleyber Torres** (37.74) was considered, but his poor matchup against Miller\u2019s elevated skill level made him an easy exclusion. We continue to monitor the status of **Cal Raleigh**, who remains out of the lineup, and **Will Smith**, who is currently on the IL, as we look to preserve our precious games-played caps for when our primary starters like **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** (56.74) are in positions to maximize their production.\n\nInvestors should remain cautious of the matchup for **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez**, who faces a stiffer test against McLean. His score is bolstered by his batting position, but the elite catcher behind the plate creates a marginal risk that forces us to temper expectations. **Lawrence Butler** (59.21) remains a viable, albeit lower-tier, play as he deals with a dynamic platoon disadvantage against Abbott. As we push toward the final stretch, we are prioritizing players who offer the best speed-power combinations, keeping an eye on depth pieces like **Masyn Winn**, **Matt Chapman**, and **Daulton Varsho** to provide relief should any of today's starters face late-game defensive substitutions or mid-game weather interference.",
